Service Role:
This service domain orchestrates the execution of the payment instruction, which may involve the coordination of  multiple steps depending on the type of payment instruction (e.g., credit transfer, direct debit, request to pay, etc.) and on whether it is an intrabank or inter-bank/overseas payment request. The steps include: 
- Invoking Payment Confirmation for internal bank policies and account eligibility checks, ensuring funds availability, verifying any customer, payment rail or counterpary preferences, performing limits checks for bank, customer and product limits as well as any payment rail specific limits, earmarking of funds in both customer's funding account and the counterparty related holding account;
- Handling payment instructions involving accounts within the bank;
- Determine fees and obtain customer approval for fees (if required, through Contact Handler);
- Handling fee transfers;
- Intelligent routing of transactions to other banks through appropriate payment schemes (considering customer preferences, SLAs, cost);
- Invoking SD-Payment Rail Operations for forwarding the Payment Instruction through the identified Payment Scheme;
- Tracking successful completion of the payment;
- Handling returns, rejects and failures;
- Initiating final funds movement by invoking SD-Payment Settlement.
- Obtain customer consent for incoming Request to Pay;
- Initiating Payment Order in response to approved Request to Pay

